        {
          "type": "turn_end",
          "turn": {
            "text": "Alberto's Fraud Detection Agent reviews newly published events and organizers on an event ticketing platform, leaving an approve/reject/request-info recommendation with reasons for a human admin. It has graded autonomy: it auto-approves only on evidence verified in code, and web sources can hold a decision back but never approve it. Offline evals showed that on a local 9B model, approved fraud fell from 54% to 8% over twelve iterations, and fraud approved without a human from 27% to 0%. Claude Haiku 5.5 was chosen for deployment: 86% accuracy vs 71%, 1% of fraud approved vs 8%. The stack includes TypeScript, PostgreSQL, and GCP.",
